                        "source_entry_id": "d621cbbe-c313-359b-ae7d-557215b8f204",
                        "source_sense_id": "f06d917d-a261-3032-b3cb-b469cfe3fa92",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mythologie: weibliches Wesen, mit einem göttlichen und einem nichtgöttlichen Elternteil",
                        "target_lang_word": "heroine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heroine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b9d13cf-13d9-38c4-b6c3-77eeefa2ac38",
                                        "entry_id": "bb6f42a7-bde9-36e8-9c14-9010c5eafde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female hero."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "946f03d6-6f75-3a3d-bf2b-259ccbb92aa0",
                                        "entry_id": "bb6f42a7-bde9-36e8-9c14-9010c5eafde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female lead character."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ee90411-cbc2-43de-8dc4-99d6961c5e46",
                                                "sense_id": "946f03d6-6f75-3a3d-bf2b-259ccbb92aa0",
                                                "text": "Miss Phyllis Morgan, as the hapless heroine dressed in the shabbiest of clothes, appears in the midst of a gay and giddy throng; she apostrophises all and sundry there, including the villain, and has a magnificent scene which always brings down the house, and nightly adds to her histrionic laurels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "heroine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab50e6d5-9879-3deb-b41a-b1013a0aff27",
                                        "entry_id": "c52cef00-00cd-3ad5-a705-d2639fa6d940",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characteristic of a heroine; heroic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62342283-5ad1-4c91-8157-d593492f40a9",
                                                "sense_id": "ab50e6d5-9879-3deb-b41a-b1013a0aff27",
                                                "text": "Theoxena to free hir Siſters children and hir owne from the laſciuious embraces of King Phillip, put weapons into their weaker hands, and perſwaded them Vt imminens ludibrium morte effugerent; to reſcue themſelues by Death from imminent diſgrace, wherein ſhe had no ſooner preuailed, but with a heroine reſolution ſhe ſhewed them by hir owne example, that what ſhee had taught them, was eaſie to be done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de631b4a-8c70-423f-815b-7166976e2976",
                                                "sense_id": "ab50e6d5-9879-3deb-b41a-b1013a0aff27",
                                                "text": "Her Brows ſoft Fur was of a paler Dye, / Conformable to that which prettily / Peep’d on her upper Lip, and cowardly / Made shew of Heroine Virility."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "625bdc14-013b-44f0-845c-15314922a459",
                                                "sense_id": "ab50e6d5-9879-3deb-b41a-b1013a0aff27",
                                                "text": "WE Your Majesties most Loyal and Dutiful Subjects do humbly crave Leave to Condole the Death of our late Gracious Sovereign, and to Congratulate Your Majesties happy Accession to the Throne of your Royal Anceſtors; as alſo to expreſs our great Satisfaction and unſpeakable Joy for the ſame, and to thank God for preſerving and quietly ſeating on the Imperial Throne of theſe Realms a Princeſs with Heart and Affections truly Engliſh, with a Zeal for the Government in Church and State as by Law Establiſhed, truly worthy of that Royal Blood that flows to you from your Royal Grandfather King Charles the Martyr, of Immortal Memory, and with a Soul truly Great and Heroine, juſtly concerned for the Proſperity of theſe Realms, and the Peace of Europe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbfc2ba8-0956-472d-8436-23fa002d7a92",
                                                "sense_id": "ab50e6d5-9879-3deb-b41a-b1013a0aff27",
                                                "text": "I had once more prevailed on Mrs. Eſten to try her York friends; ſhe rather wiſhed to avoid the hazard, as ſhe rightly judged ſhe had been treated ſo very negligently, after a profuſion of praiſe and promiſe; however from my ſolicitation ſhe did break through her heroine reſolution, and once more on her return from Scotland ventured her little bark to the generoſity and pleaſure of her profeſſed friends at York."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45c61272-ead9-49fd-91d6-715d5332cc32",
                                                "sense_id": "ab50e6d5-9879-3deb-b41a-b1013a0aff27",
                                                "text": "How otherwise than by a violation of a pledge could he have conquered Limerick, protected as it then was by the heroine bravery of its defenders."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc8002bb-23d7-4411-ba29-d3fc633e78b9",
                        "source_entry_id": "d621cbbe-c313-359b-ae7d-557215b8f204",
                        "source_sense_id": "f06d917d-a261-3032-b3cb-b469cfe3fa92",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mythologie: weibliches Wesen, mit einem göttlichen und einem nichtgöttlichen Elternteil",
                        "target_lang_word": "héroïne",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "héroïne",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3b3316b-7b54-309e-bddf-babfc0b3a690",
                                        "entry_id": "c932b239-8a54-32fd-88d2-c285278e595c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Femme courageuse qui a de l’élévation et de la noblesse dans les sentiments, dans la conduite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9be12c5d-feee-4b50-9347-901b8181e166",
                                                "sense_id": "a3b3316b-7b54-309e-bddf-babfc0b3a690",
                                                "text": "C’était au lendemain du prix Goncourt. La gauche germanopratine frissonnait d’aise. Elle avait trouvé un nouveau héros. Une nouvelle héroïne, plutôt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbd4255b-5498-3617-b035-30b88eea3685",
                                        "entry_id": "c932b239-8a54-32fd-88d2-c285278e595c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celle dont on raconte ou dont on représente la vie, les aventures, les actions, dans un conte, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bf31551-cc06-48df-a150-43ee10e24aa2",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd4255b-5498-3617-b035-30b88eea3685",
                                                "text": "Devenue en idée l’héroïne d’un roman pareil, plus d’une fois elle étudia le rôle sublime d’Eliza."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59872052-8ada-4809-a592-a91a53c950bb",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd4255b-5498-3617-b035-30b88eea3685",
                                                "text": "Une heure auparavant, j’avais cru que Mauricette serait l’héroïne de mon aventure… Sa mère m’enflammait dix fois davantage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "021a8fc4-f9c7-4c61-80f9-30941156b248",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd4255b-5498-3617-b035-30b88eea3685",
                                                "text": "Tout incitait donc un auteur de romans, à l’époque où Jane Austen commençait à écrire les siens, à dépeindre une héroïne à la santé fragile et à la beauté délicate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4caf3f83-ab46-4943-8571-7e9b309171bd",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd4255b-5498-3617-b035-30b88eea3685",
                                                "text": "Elle aurait pu être une héroïne durassienne déambulant, l’air mélancolique, dans la touffeur d’un penthouse tropical."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "héroïne",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a744c63a-96ce-3aa1-9061-a371ff1457e0",
                                        "entry_id": "974993d2-6d9d-3384-b467-be70217caab8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Drogue dure dérivée de la morphine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84bb563f-4478-4169-9c82-f1dd9ff17b4f",
                                                "sense_id": "a744c63a-96ce-3aa1-9061-a371ff1457e0",
                                                "text": "Il avait découvert l’héroïne dont il avait été surpris et séduit. Au fond, il avait cru pendant quelque temps au paradis sur la terre. Maintenant cette illusion éphémère lui faisait hausser les épaules."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ea17140-8219-408c-9ea1-454dc79f933e",
                                                "sense_id": "a744c63a-96ce-3aa1-9061-a371ff1457e0",
                                                "text": "Le second de ces personnages est un médecin marron, qui s’était fait pincer deux fois dans un trafic d’héroïne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0775fd05-0727-4a21-aafd-556cfa29c95f",
                                                "sense_id": "a744c63a-96ce-3aa1-9061-a371ff1457e0",
                                                "text": "Et Monk agit comme un déclic : le saxophoniste décroche de l’héroïne, cold turkey, comme disent les Américains, c’est-à-dire du jour au lendemain. Dinde froide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ce3a33a-99aa-49cf-a383-b7193cbcfacb",
                                                "sense_id": "a744c63a-96ce-3aa1-9061-a371ff1457e0",
                                                "text": "Très vite, le lien entre ce que voulait dire Motörhead, ou speedfreak, c'est-à-dire quelqu'un qui carbure aux amphétamines et surtout pas aux drogues dures de type héroïne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
